1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,166
What we need here is a magical typewriter.

2
00:00:03,167 --> 00:00:04,436
What do you think?

3
00:00:04,436 --> 00:00:05,968
Savana, what do you think?

4
00:00:05,968 --> 00:00:09,623
I'm sorry, Liam,
but we're not doing a fantasy film.

5
00:00:12,546 --> 00:00:13,911
Turn your back.

6
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:16,667
Borj, let's get Tristan in the room.

7
00:00:16,667 --> 00:00:19,266
- Oh, come on...
- Deedee, please delete the video.

8
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:20,734
Why would I do that?

9
00:00:20,734 --> 00:00:23,700
I'm going to sell this.

10
00:00:23,701 --> 00:00:24,622
Love.

11
00:00:24,622 --> 00:00:26,427
Joyce...

12
00:00:27,877 --> 00:00:28,745
Joyce.

13
00:00:28,745 --> 00:00:30,562
<i>Savana's video while drunk dancing in a club</i>

14
00:00:30,562 --> 00:00:35,567
<i>is now viral on social media.</i>

15
00:00:35,567 --> 00:00:36,601
Savana.

16
00:00:36,601 --> 00:00:37,759
Hans.

17
00:00:38,903 --> 00:00:41,999
I came back
as soon I saw the video sent by my friend.

18
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:42,941
How are you feeling?

19
00:00:42,941 --> 00:00:44,509
Have you talked to Aunt Joanne already?

20
00:00:44,509 --> 00:00:45,744
I will hear it from you now.

21
00:00:45,744 --> 00:00:48,380
You were captured on video while drinking!

22
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:53,918
Can't you see or feel
that I need even just a little space, Mom?

23
00:00:53,918 --> 00:00:57,689
If I had let you decide for yourself,

24
00:00:57,689 --> 00:01:00,257
you would have probably
lost your career already.

25
00:01:14,172 --> 00:01:17,842
Everyone, let's proceed
to the conference room.

26
00:01:17,842 --> 00:01:22,470
I'm sorry
that our meeting coincided with the audition.

27
00:01:23,281 --> 00:01:25,050
Let's go?

28
00:01:25,050 --> 00:01:26,401
Here, this way.

29
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:37,162
Boss bro.

30
00:01:37,863 --> 00:01:40,699
Congressman's new protégé is so cocky.

31
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:44,701
Looks like
the meeting will be more action-packed

32
00:01:44,701 --> 00:01:48,208
than the auditions.

33
00:01:48,208 --> 00:01:50,333
You and your big mouth.

34
00:01:50,334 --> 00:01:53,136
You better help Megan

35
00:01:53,136 --> 00:01:55,882
since Leroy and Deedee are
on emergency leave.

36
00:01:55,882 --> 00:01:58,385
Where is it?
Over there? Should I follow them?

37
00:01:58,385 --> 00:02:01,353
- Of course.
- Okay, Boss Bro.

38
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:09,460
Congressman Ramon's team has decided
to replace Tristan

39
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:12,435
because he only has a 50-50 chance
of winning the elections.

40
00:02:12,435 --> 00:02:16,001
So, Josh will run for Congress.

41
00:02:16,903 --> 00:02:19,072
And because we can't afford to lose,

42
00:02:19,072 --> 00:02:22,338
the Congressman's PR team
raised a big concern

43
00:02:22,338 --> 00:02:25,010
about our movie production.

44
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:30,116
He doesn't want
to get associated with Savana anymore.

45
00:02:41,059 --> 00:02:45,730
You all know why we're making this movie
before the elections.

46
00:02:46,433 --> 00:02:50,837
We don't want to give the voters,
especially the rivals,

47
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:54,941
a weapon to destroy our candidate.

48
00:02:54,941 --> 00:02:57,644
Excuse me. Excuse me, Sir Vergil.

49
00:02:57,644 --> 00:03:00,981
Let's get straight to the point.

50
00:03:00,981 --> 00:03:04,617
Is this because of Savana's viral video?

51
00:03:04,617 --> 00:03:07,053
We already issued a statement.

52
00:03:07,053 --> 00:03:09,622
We also did an interview.

53
00:03:09,622 --> 00:03:11,358
Didn't you watch it?

54
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:12,392
Here!

55
00:03:12,392 --> 00:03:14,326
- Here it is!
- Mommy.

56
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:21,094
Savana...

57
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:26,180
Your video getting wild in a bar
is far from your image.

58
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:33,313
I'm sure Blacksmith isn't
the only one reacting to this scandal.

59
00:03:33,313 --> 00:03:36,549
What does your TV network say?

60
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:40,387
The products that you endorse?

61
00:03:40,387 --> 00:03:45,530
Do you think the damage control
you and your mother did was enough?

62
00:03:49,362 --> 00:03:50,967
VLH...

63
00:04:08,214 --> 00:04:10,167
In this industry,

64
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:13,327
we sometimes encounter problems
we cannot overcome.

65
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,928
Like what, VLH?

66
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:28,666
The bashing and cyberbullying of Savana?

67
00:04:29,869 --> 00:04:33,639
Should we get affected by those things?

68
00:04:34,705 --> 00:04:40,713
Shouldn't we focus on what matters more?

69
00:04:40,713 --> 00:04:45,085
And that is to create a good movie
regardless of the issues thrown at us.

70
00:04:45,085 --> 00:04:47,887
Issues that have
nothing to do with our project.

71
00:04:48,941 --> 00:04:51,624
You don't know anything
about this industry, Liam.

72
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:53,393
Why don't you just go back to Casa Fuerte?

73
00:04:53,393 --> 00:04:55,929
Weren't you the ones
who dumped me here in Blacksmith?

74
00:04:55,929 --> 00:05:00,066
It's my right to protect this project.

75
00:05:00,066 --> 00:05:01,834
That's enough.

76
00:05:12,178 --> 00:05:14,481
I will let the Congressman decide.

77
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:16,950
This is not just about the movie.

78
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:20,085
This is also about Josh's bid for Congress.

79
00:06:04,697 --> 00:06:06,839
Let's take a break.

80
00:06:39,605 --> 00:06:43,536
I know how cutthroat showbiz is.

81
00:06:43,536 --> 00:06:47,540
But... I still get surprised.

82
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:50,376
Your issues seem to be on schedule.

83
00:06:50,376 --> 00:06:52,588
You have new issues every day.

84
00:06:52,588 --> 00:06:54,346
Different issues.

85
00:06:56,549 --> 00:06:58,657
I hope you're okay.

86
00:07:02,643 --> 00:07:04,564
I'm used to it.

87
00:07:07,119 --> 00:07:11,581
Actually, my past issues were worse.

88
00:07:13,566 --> 00:07:17,102
I used to get affected by it. But now...

89
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:24,944
Are you and your mom okay?

90
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:28,414
I know how strong her personality is.

91
00:07:29,304 --> 00:07:34,075
I mean... for sure,
you two can get through this.

92
00:07:42,395 --> 00:07:44,530
Thank you for the pep talk.

93
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:50,602
It was great working with you, Mr. Herrera.

94
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:53,806
What?

95
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:56,309
I know the drill.

96
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:58,944
I'm sure I'm getting axed.

97
00:07:59,728 --> 00:08:02,564
It's so easy to replace actors.

98
00:08:25,350 --> 00:08:31,010
<i>Joyce, if only I could take away your burden,</i>

99
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:32,622
<i>I would do it.</i>

100
00:08:41,581 --> 00:08:43,325
Mr. Herrera.

101
00:08:44,067 --> 00:08:46,402
It was great working with you.

102
00:09:13,613 --> 00:09:16,953
We'll proceed with Josh and Savana's film.

103
00:09:17,867 --> 00:09:20,961
Savana will remain as
the film's leading lady.

104
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:38,177
Joanne...

105
00:09:38,177 --> 00:09:40,113
this is the men's restroom.

106
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:42,715
I know, Congressman.

107
00:09:42,715 --> 00:09:47,520
Oh, Congressman... about your other godson...

108
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:50,286
Is he sure about his identity?

109
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,802
Oh my God.

110
00:10:02,802 --> 00:10:05,705
Look. He's dancing.

111
00:10:05,705 --> 00:10:06,837
It's so funny.

112
00:10:06,837 --> 00:10:09,384
Look.

113
00:10:09,384 --> 00:10:12,545
- Look.
- Friend, look.

114
00:10:12,545 --> 00:10:14,647
He's dancing his heart out.

115
00:10:14,647 --> 00:10:16,983
Look.

116
00:10:16,983 --> 00:10:19,619
- Look at that.
- Hey, what's that?

117
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,821
What's that? Let me see it.

118
00:10:21,821 --> 00:10:23,623
- What's that?
- Nothing.

119
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:26,033
I said let me see. Give it to me.

120
00:10:35,968 --> 00:10:37,737
Please send it to me. Hurry.

121
00:10:37,737 --> 00:10:39,138
Send it to me.

122
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,740
- Sorry?
- Send it to me

123
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:43,242
if you don't want to lose your job
here in my resort.

124
00:10:43,242 --> 00:10:44,577
Send it to me right now.

125
00:10:44,577 --> 00:10:45,756
Okay.

126
00:10:47,847 --> 00:10:49,345
I've already sent it.

127
00:10:57,087 --> 00:11:01,327
<i>Why are you getting him drunk? Look at him.</i>

128
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:04,596
Okay, get back to work.

129
00:11:20,879 --> 00:11:24,281
I'll let you and your daughter
win this round.

130
00:11:27,954 --> 00:11:29,513
Excuse me.

131
00:12:00,537 --> 00:12:02,834
Thank you, Liam.

132
00:12:02,834 --> 00:12:07,159
Thank you for not giving up on this project.

133
00:12:09,412 --> 00:12:14,100
Thank you for not letting
the issues against me affect you.

134
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,435
All's well that ends well, right?

135
00:12:16,435 --> 00:12:18,537
I can now relax.

136
00:12:19,712 --> 00:12:21,213
How about you?

137
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:24,650
I'm happy that we're still doing the project.

138
00:12:25,689 --> 00:12:29,767
I just wonder why
the congressman didn't replace me.

139
00:12:31,295 --> 00:12:34,397
Savana, are you coming home with me?

140
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:37,256
No, Mommy.

141
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:39,586
Hans and I still need to go somewhere.

142
00:12:40,383 --> 00:12:41,594
Okay.

143
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:45,095
I'm done with work today, anyway.

144
00:12:50,269 --> 00:12:52,104
I'll go ahead.

145
00:12:57,743 --> 00:13:01,113
<i>Joyce, after all the wrong things I've done,</i>

146
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:05,517
<i>all I can do now is stay by your side.</i>

147
00:13:12,224 --> 00:13:14,058
Excuse me.

148
00:13:14,058 --> 00:13:17,161
I'm sorry, Miss Via.
I know we're swamped with work,

149
00:13:17,161 --> 00:13:20,486
but I already found the woman
you wanted me to research about.

150
00:13:20,486 --> 00:13:22,806
The woman named Joycelyn Trinidad.

151
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:31,677
You can leave for now, Nicole.

152
00:13:31,677 --> 00:13:32,898
Okay.

153
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:41,187
So...

154
00:13:56,133 --> 00:14:02,434
[Trinidad Joycelyn Cruz]

155
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:05,778
Actually, there are a lot of permutations.

156
00:14:05,778 --> 00:14:11,017
There is Jocelyn, Joycely,
and Joyce Marie Trinidad.

157
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:14,787
But this is the only Joycelyn Trinidad
we found.

158
00:14:14,787 --> 00:14:18,290
I had to convince my ex-boyfriend who's a cop
to give me that.

159
00:14:26,832 --> 00:14:30,136
So, she's been a domestic helper in France
for 30 years now.

160
00:14:30,136 --> 00:14:31,702
She's a bit old.

161
00:14:31,702 --> 00:14:34,320
Probably that's why we can't find her
on the internet.

162
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:36,542
Probably, she's not too techie.

163
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:38,543
Is she the one you're looking for?

164
00:14:43,916 --> 00:14:48,320
If you don't mind me asking, Miss...
who is she?

165
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:49,555
Is she a distant relative?

166
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:54,586
Or a former housemaid that you want to help?

167
00:14:54,586 --> 00:14:56,258
Who is she?

168
00:15:00,032 --> 00:15:01,399
No.

169
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:04,569
I don't think she's the one I'm looking for.

170
00:15:05,436 --> 00:15:06,671
Sorry, Miss Via.

171
00:15:06,671 --> 00:15:08,681
I probably missed something.

172
00:15:08,681 --> 00:15:09,839
I'll keep looking.

173
00:15:09,839 --> 00:15:11,478
Please.

174
00:15:24,955 --> 00:15:30,129
Sir Liam, here's the fight director's
body of work.

175
00:15:30,129 --> 00:15:33,599
He's actually trained by a Chinese director,

176
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:36,602
who is also an expert in martial arts movies.

177
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:38,308
So here it is.

178
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:43,942
Savana...

179
00:15:46,345 --> 00:15:49,084
Are you coming home with me?

180
00:15:49,084 --> 00:15:50,949
No, Mom.

181
00:15:50,949 --> 00:15:52,975
Hans and I still need to go somewhere.

182
00:15:54,264 --> 00:15:55,920
Sir Liam?

183
00:15:56,955 --> 00:15:58,190
Yeah.

184
00:15:58,190 --> 00:16:02,661
Well, if Phil and the rest of the team
already approved it,

185
00:16:02,661 --> 00:16:05,297
we can already set a meeting with him.

186
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:07,131
Okay, Sir.

187
00:16:08,667 --> 00:16:10,169
Can I see it?

188
00:16:10,169 --> 00:16:11,663
Here.

189
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:21,113
Maybe we can use Savana's meltdown
for publicity

190
00:16:21,113 --> 00:16:23,649
if we're not replacing her.

191
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:26,318
We can parallel it
to her character in the movie.

192
00:16:26,318 --> 00:16:30,013
I think her character will have a fall
from grace, right?

193
00:16:30,013 --> 00:16:33,157
It's perfect
for what she's going through right now.

194
00:16:37,963 --> 00:16:40,098
- This one.
- Liam.

195
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,203
Can we talk?

196
00:16:44,203 --> 00:16:46,071
Yes, Uncle.

197
00:16:46,071 --> 00:16:47,906
Excuse me, Sir.

198
00:16:47,906 --> 00:16:49,284
Sir.

199
00:16:53,947 --> 00:17:00,753
How does it feel to encounter problems
early on with the production?

200
00:17:02,307 --> 00:17:05,023
Are you talking about Savana, Uncle?

201
00:17:05,023 --> 00:17:07,059
Well, she's a strong woman.

202
00:17:07,059 --> 00:17:10,562
So I know
she won't let the issues affect her.

203
00:17:10,562 --> 00:17:13,508
And about our film,

204
00:17:13,508 --> 00:17:17,236
we hope the audience will still accept it

205
00:17:17,236 --> 00:17:19,837
without bias against the actors.

206
00:17:21,445 --> 00:17:24,704
Are you really serious about this?

207
00:17:25,509 --> 00:17:27,533
What?

208
00:17:27,534 --> 00:17:29,048
Of course, Uncle.

209
00:17:29,049 --> 00:17:33,486
This is the chance my dad gave me
to prove myself.

210
00:17:34,695 --> 00:17:37,197
I don't think you understand.

211
00:17:39,258 --> 00:17:44,366
I let Danilo put you here in Blacksmith
to lie low.

212
00:17:44,367 --> 00:17:48,367
People have their eyes on you at Casa Fuerte.

213
00:17:48,367 --> 00:17:51,536
But we cannot totally lose you there.

214
00:17:54,139 --> 00:17:59,778
Uncle, I thought
you and Dad entrusted me with this film?

215
00:17:59,778 --> 00:18:01,980
Of course!

216
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:08,519
I want Josh to win a seat in congress
through this film.

217
00:18:09,788 --> 00:18:12,724
But Vergil can do this.

218
00:18:12,724 --> 00:18:15,260
I'm already invested in this project, Uncle.

219
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,229
This is also my dream.

220
00:18:17,229 --> 00:18:20,647
I don't think you understand, Liam!

221
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:29,675
What the hell are you talking about, Liam?

222
00:18:29,675 --> 00:18:32,577
You sound like a different person!

223
00:18:37,983 --> 00:18:40,752
Get your act together!

224
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:42,701
I let you deal

225
00:18:42,701 --> 00:18:46,399
with whatever mid-life crisis
you're going through!

226
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:48,860
But when I say
you will return to Casa Fuerte,

227
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,329
you will!

228
00:18:50,329 --> 00:18:52,296
Do you understand?

229
00:19:17,089 --> 00:19:19,358
I'll tell you something.

230
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:29,719
A part of me thinks
it's a blessing in disguise

231
00:19:29,719 --> 00:19:32,403
if you lose your project in Blacksmith.

232
00:19:39,828 --> 00:19:43,164
What made you think that?

233
00:19:44,356 --> 00:19:46,616
You know me.

234
00:19:46,616 --> 00:19:52,980
When you said
your movie is a little physically demanding,

235
00:19:52,980 --> 00:19:55,257
I couldn't help but worry.

236
00:19:59,563 --> 00:20:02,064
Hans, this is my dream project.

237
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:07,570
I'm so tired of doing unchallenging roles.

238
00:20:08,238 --> 00:20:11,495
I always portray a damsel in distress
who needs to be saved by the hero.

239
00:20:11,495 --> 00:20:13,562
I don't want anything like that anymore.

240
00:20:16,603 --> 00:20:18,415
And besides, I'm happy with Blacksmith.

241
00:20:18,415 --> 00:20:20,282
Because in Blacksmith...

242
00:20:21,941 --> 00:20:25,277
they listen to my opinion,

243
00:20:25,922 --> 00:20:28,657
my suggestions, ideas... everything.

244
00:20:30,827 --> 00:20:33,597
Blacksmith knows how to make action films.

245
00:20:33,597 --> 00:20:35,865
It's not a big deal, actually.

246
00:20:35,865 --> 00:20:38,768
But if Liam can assure your safety,

247
00:20:38,768 --> 00:20:41,003
I won't have a problem with it.

248
00:20:42,190 --> 00:20:44,391
I'm just worried.

249
00:20:58,388 --> 00:21:00,957
Hi, Savana. Can I have a picture with you?

250
00:21:00,957 --> 00:21:03,693
Is it okay?

251
00:21:03,693 --> 00:21:05,962
- I'll do it. I'll take your picture.
- Thank you.

252
00:21:05,962 --> 00:21:07,163
- No problem.
- Thank you.

253
00:21:07,163 --> 00:21:08,965
Thank you.

254
00:21:08,965 --> 00:21:12,302
Okay. One, two...

255
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:15,305
- Okay.
- Thank you so much.

256
00:21:15,305 --> 00:21:17,964
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

257
00:21:18,975 --> 00:21:21,811
Hey. Isn't that Savana?

258
00:21:21,811 --> 00:21:23,713
Have you seen her video?

259
00:21:23,713 --> 00:21:25,081
She was so drunk.

260
00:21:25,081 --> 00:21:26,883
She was out of control.

261
00:21:26,883 --> 00:21:30,827
Yes. She said nasty things about her mother.

262
00:21:30,827 --> 00:21:32,489
I used to like her so much.

263
00:21:32,489 --> 00:21:35,426
I even wished to have a daughter like her.

264
00:21:35,426 --> 00:21:38,702
But now, I know what kind of daughter
she really is.

265
00:21:38,702 --> 00:21:39,829
Ungrateful.

266
00:21:39,829 --> 00:21:40,864
Right.

267
00:21:40,864 --> 00:21:44,538
I will probably disown her
if she's my daughter.

268
00:21:55,346 --> 00:21:57,147
Sorry...

269
00:22:11,861 --> 00:22:13,762
Do you want to go somewhere else?

270
00:22:17,367 --> 00:22:18,983
Sir!

271
00:22:21,571 --> 00:22:22,806
Bill out, please.

272
00:22:22,806 --> 00:22:23,807
We're going to bill out.

273
00:22:23,807 --> 00:22:25,241
- I'm going to get your bill.
- No need.

274
00:22:25,241 --> 00:22:27,243
It's okay. Here's the money.

275
00:22:29,813 --> 00:22:31,915
Sir, this is too much.

276
00:22:31,915 --> 00:22:33,483
It's okay. You can have the rest, okay?

277
00:22:33,483 --> 00:22:36,465
I'm sorry we're in a hurry. Thank you.

278
00:22:36,465 --> 00:22:38,599
Where are we going?

279
00:22:39,629 --> 00:22:41,762
Just follow me, come on.

280
00:22:43,426 --> 00:22:45,461
She walked out.

281
00:22:46,730 --> 00:22:48,264
I know the head chef here.

282
00:22:48,264 --> 00:22:52,168
I'm sure you'll enjoy the food.

283
00:22:52,168 --> 00:22:54,370
Where's the chef? Chef!

284
00:22:57,273 --> 00:22:58,808
Hans.

285
00:22:58,808 --> 00:22:59,843
How are you, bro?

286
00:22:59,843 --> 00:23:01,745
- Chef JR! Nice to see you.
- How are you?

287
00:23:01,745 --> 00:23:03,433
- Nice to see you. I'm good.
- How's life?

288
00:23:03,434 --> 00:23:07,533
Thank you, looks like you already
have food prepared for us.

289
00:23:07,534 --> 00:23:08,852
No problem.

290
00:23:08,852 --> 00:23:11,254
- We don't have privacy at the other cafe.
- I understand.

291
00:23:11,254 --> 00:23:13,633
By the way, do I still have to introduce her?

292
00:23:13,634 --> 00:23:16,867
Of course, I know you.

293
00:23:16,868 --> 00:23:18,099
- Hi.
- Savana.

294
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:20,533
- Hello.
- My name's JR.

295
00:23:20,534 --> 00:23:23,635
Please, have a seat.

296
00:23:23,636 --> 00:23:24,602
Savana.

297
00:23:24,603 --> 00:23:26,668
We serve nothing but the best.

298
00:23:26,669 --> 00:23:29,438
I will let you try my specialty.

299
00:23:37,115 --> 00:23:39,600
Looks like it will be a cheat day.

300
00:23:50,696 --> 00:23:52,532
Ladies first.

301
00:23:52,533 --> 00:23:54,468
Here you go, Ma'am.

302
00:23:55,702 --> 00:23:57,343
- Bro.
- Thank you.

303
00:23:58,079 --> 00:23:59,004
Enjoy your meal.

304
00:23:59,006 --> 00:24:01,174
- I'll come back later.
- Thank you.

305
00:24:02,499 --> 00:24:04,124
Remember, you're on a diet.

306
00:24:05,048 --> 00:24:08,317
- Be careful.
- Hans, please. Just today.

307
00:24:09,665 --> 00:24:11,106
Go ahead.

308
00:24:11,107 --> 00:24:12,659
Round two?

309
00:24:37,006 --> 00:24:39,242
So you heard it right from Uncle Ramon.

310
00:24:39,242 --> 00:24:42,846
He and Dad agreed to let me babysit you.

311
00:24:42,846 --> 00:24:45,815
And now you're imposing yourself here.

312
00:24:45,815 --> 00:24:50,653
All our lives,
you're the best in everyone's eyes.

313
00:24:53,490 --> 00:24:57,494
Why does Uncle Ramon talk
like he has more authority than dad?

314
00:24:57,494 --> 00:24:59,329
What the...

315
00:25:00,631 --> 00:25:02,966
Have you already forgotten?

316
00:25:02,966 --> 00:25:05,935
We don't talk about things like that!

317
00:25:07,671 --> 00:25:09,354
Oh, Liam!

318
00:25:09,354 --> 00:25:12,609
You really have gone insane!

319
00:25:14,545 --> 00:25:18,611
Fine. Even though I don't like you,
I will let it slide just this once.

320
00:25:20,558 --> 00:25:25,496
I will pretend you forgot
that Uncle Ramon owns us.

321
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:28,776
What do you mean he owns us?

322
00:25:29,493 --> 00:25:31,394
Go on. Make it louder!

323
00:25:39,901 --> 00:25:43,905
Blacksmith Productions, Casa Fuerte,

324
00:25:43,905 --> 00:25:46,307
and our other businesses are his.

325
00:25:46,307 --> 00:25:52,713
We're lucky Congressman Ramon
lets us take care of his businesses.

326
00:25:54,205 --> 00:25:57,252
He'll bring us with him to the top.

327
00:25:57,252 --> 00:26:01,757
So, you can go against everyone
except Congressman Ramon.

328
00:26:01,757 --> 00:26:03,991
If you do that, you'll get what you deserve.

329
00:26:04,677 --> 00:26:06,912
What you did in Casa Fuerte...

330
00:26:08,323 --> 00:26:11,569
you're lucky
because his daughter is your girlfriend.

331
00:26:11,569 --> 00:26:16,707
If not, he would have buried you alive.

332
00:26:22,145 --> 00:26:24,414
Get out of here.

333
00:26:24,414 --> 00:26:27,089
I don't want to get in trouble
because of you.

334
00:26:27,089 --> 00:26:28,890
Leave!

335
00:26:57,647 --> 00:26:58,715
There.

336
00:26:58,715 --> 00:27:00,984
How are you, guys?

337
00:27:00,984 --> 00:27:02,352
Just a little something for you.

338
00:27:02,352 --> 00:27:03,753
- Bring it home with you.
- Chef, thank you.

339
00:27:03,753 --> 00:27:05,655
I'll bring it home.

340
00:27:05,655 --> 00:27:09,225
Her mother might scold her
if she sees her eating this.

341
00:27:09,225 --> 00:27:11,160
Chef, your food is so good.

342
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:12,528
Thank you so much.

343
00:27:12,528 --> 00:27:13,997
My pleasure, my pleasure.

344
00:27:13,997 --> 00:27:16,032
I will expect you guys to come back, okay?

345
00:27:16,032 --> 00:27:17,166
Yes, Chef.

346
00:27:17,166 --> 00:27:20,937
Looks like I'm going to be
your regular customer.

347
00:27:20,937 --> 00:27:22,271
I'll look forward to it.

348
00:27:22,271 --> 00:27:23,333
Okay.

349
00:27:23,334 --> 00:27:25,848
Bro, nice to see you. Thank you again.

350
00:27:25,849 --> 00:27:29,445
I hope she's already your girlfriend
the next time you visit.

351
00:27:29,445 --> 00:27:31,127
I hope so, too.

352
00:27:32,181 --> 00:27:33,638
Let's go?

353
00:27:36,914 --> 00:27:38,648
Thank you.

354
00:27:43,997 --> 00:27:45,897
Sorry.

355
00:27:57,963 --> 00:27:59,409
Are you okay?

356
00:27:59,409 --> 00:28:00,410
Are you hurt?

357
00:28:00,410 --> 00:28:02,611
I'm okay.

358
00:28:03,780 --> 00:28:05,782
Let's go.

359
00:28:05,782 --> 00:28:07,306
Hans...

360
00:28:09,260 --> 00:28:12,563
Can you give me time alone?

361
00:28:14,323 --> 00:28:16,092
I'll just book a ride home.

362
00:28:16,092 --> 00:28:19,294
There's somewhere I need to drop by first.

363
00:28:23,434 --> 00:28:26,269
- Are you sure?
- I'm sure.

364
00:28:27,438 --> 00:28:29,572
Don't worry about me.

365
00:28:30,272 --> 00:28:32,176
Okay.

366
00:28:32,176 --> 00:28:34,979
Be safe, okay?

367
00:28:34,979 --> 00:28:36,373
Okay, see you.

368
00:28:40,418 --> 00:28:42,187
I had fun. Thank you.

369
00:28:42,187 --> 00:28:44,589
Thanks to you, too.

370
00:28:44,589 --> 00:28:46,490
Okay, bye.

371
00:28:47,226 --> 00:28:49,195
I'll get going.

372
00:28:49,195 --> 00:28:51,363
Okay. Be safe, okay?

373
00:29:12,282 --> 00:29:13,750
Hi, Mom.

374
00:29:13,750 --> 00:29:15,003
Son.

375
00:29:17,955 --> 00:29:20,725
Wow, where are we going?

376
00:29:20,725 --> 00:29:22,993
Looks like we're going on a vacation.

377
00:29:24,028 --> 00:29:26,564
Just me.

378
00:29:26,564 --> 00:29:28,665
Why are you not bringing me with you?

379
00:29:29,934 --> 00:29:34,038
If I can do that, why not?

380
00:29:34,038 --> 00:29:39,977
I'm already used to traveling alone
on my birthday.

381
00:29:42,113 --> 00:29:45,415
Is it because
I was busy with work in Casa Fuerte?

382
00:29:47,718 --> 00:29:51,756
Son, I'm not forcing you to come with me.

383
00:29:51,756 --> 00:29:57,828
I've long accepted that you're always busy.

384
00:29:59,263 --> 00:30:02,433
We owe Casa Fuerte a lot.

385
00:30:02,433 --> 00:30:03,934
You wouldn't be able to pay for my operation

386
00:30:03,934 --> 00:30:07,304
if it wasn't for your job, right?

387
00:30:08,239 --> 00:30:14,412
So it's okay with you that

388
00:30:14,412 --> 00:30:17,047
I'm not there on special occasions
like your birthday?

389
00:30:19,016 --> 00:30:21,519
Who knows?

390
00:30:21,519 --> 00:30:25,054
Since you're no longer in Casa Fuerte,

391
00:30:25,054 --> 00:30:30,527
you might be able to come with me again
on my birthday. Right?

392
00:30:32,763 --> 00:30:34,664
Ouch.

393
00:30:38,102 --> 00:30:41,071
Mom, are you okay?

394
00:30:51,223 --> 00:30:57,655
Son, won't the doctor get mad
that you brought me out?

395
00:30:57,655 --> 00:30:59,590
Mom...

396
00:30:59,590 --> 00:31:02,092
I want you to be happy.

397
00:31:03,498 --> 00:31:05,499
Happy birthday, Mom.

398
00:31:06,797 --> 00:31:09,433
Thank you, son.

399
00:31:09,433 --> 00:31:12,702
But you don't have to do this.

400
00:31:13,972 --> 00:31:15,537
Mom...

401
00:31:18,843 --> 00:31:21,405
You know I can't do that.

402
00:31:22,279 --> 00:31:24,648
This day is special.

403
00:31:24,648 --> 00:31:26,783
Because it's your birthday.

404
00:31:29,190 --> 00:31:31,191
Special...

405
00:31:33,290 --> 00:31:36,794
Because it may be
my last birthday celebration.

406
00:31:36,794 --> 00:31:38,895
Come on, Mom.

407
00:31:40,364 --> 00:31:44,502
I don't want you saying things like that.

408
00:31:44,502 --> 00:31:46,556
Mom...

409
00:31:46,556 --> 00:31:48,339
Mom, you'll get better.

410
00:31:50,274 --> 00:31:54,378
And you'll still celebrate
many birthdays with me,

411
00:31:54,378 --> 00:31:56,280
my wife, and my son.

412
00:31:56,280 --> 00:31:57,747
Okay?

413
00:31:59,181 --> 00:32:01,015
I love you.

414
00:32:06,958 --> 00:32:09,519
One, two, three, go.

415
00:32:09,519 --> 00:32:12,730
- Happy birthday, Mama Tess!
- Happy birthday.

416
00:32:12,730 --> 00:32:15,399
- Happy birthday, Grandma.
- Happy birthday.

417
00:32:15,399 --> 00:32:17,368
Happy birthday, Grandma.

418
00:32:17,368 --> 00:32:19,170
Give Grandma a kiss.

419
00:32:19,170 --> 00:32:22,139
Mama Tess, happy birthday.

420
00:32:22,139 --> 00:32:23,474
You got that, Hon?

421
00:32:23,474 --> 00:32:25,509
- There you go.
- Of course.

422
00:32:25,509 --> 00:32:28,556
- Mama Tess, make a wish.
- Make a wish first.

423
00:32:28,556 --> 00:32:31,494
One, two, three...

424
00:32:32,850 --> 00:32:34,518
- Yay!
- Yay!

425
00:32:34,518 --> 00:32:35,753
Happy birthday, Mom.

426
00:32:35,753 --> 00:32:37,388
Happy birthday, Grandma.

427
00:32:37,388 --> 00:32:41,258
Thank you for the overflowing love.

428
00:32:41,258 --> 00:32:43,561
We love you so much.

429
00:32:43,561 --> 00:32:45,196
- I love you, Mom.
- I love you, Mama Tess.

430
00:32:45,196 --> 00:32:48,232
- Happy birthday, Grandma.
- Thank you.

431
00:32:48,232 --> 00:32:50,666
- My grandson.
- Happy birthday.

432
00:32:50,666 --> 00:32:52,169
We love you.

433
00:32:52,169 --> 00:32:54,111
Dance for grandma.

434
00:32:54,111 --> 00:32:55,239
Dance, come on.

435
00:32:55,239 --> 00:32:57,486
- Come here, dear.
- Show grandma your dance.

436
00:32:57,486 --> 00:32:59,767
- Ready, set, go!
- Show her.

437
00:32:59,767 --> 00:33:07,117
Happy birthday, happy birthday,
happy birthday, Grandma!

438
00:33:07,117 --> 00:33:11,221
Happy birthday, Grandma.

439
00:33:12,932 --> 00:33:14,659
Yes, son.

440
00:33:15,312 --> 00:33:17,747
I just had a mild headache.

441
00:33:20,464 --> 00:33:27,103
Maybe I've been on the gadget for too long.

442
00:33:27,872 --> 00:33:32,042
I told you. You should get some rest, Mom.

443
00:33:32,042 --> 00:33:36,179
You better go to your room.
Get some rest for now.

444
00:33:37,154 --> 00:33:39,322
- Okay.
- Let's go.

445
00:33:55,733 --> 00:33:57,101
Hello, Mom?

446
00:33:57,101 --> 00:33:59,803
Sorry, I can't talk right now.

447
00:33:59,803 --> 00:34:00,863
<i>Savana, where are you?</i>

448
00:34:00,863 --> 00:34:03,841
<i>Why am I hearing crickets?</i>

449
00:34:03,841 --> 00:34:05,781
I'm at a spa right now.

450
00:34:05,781 --> 00:34:09,246
It's the ambient sound.

451
00:34:09,246 --> 00:34:11,282
I'll call you back. Bye.

452
00:34:20,325 --> 00:34:21,844
Hey!

453
00:34:24,807 --> 00:34:26,741
Are you okay?

454
00:34:30,467 --> 00:34:31,705
Dad...

455
00:34:32,551 --> 00:34:34,135
Let's go home.

456
00:34:40,077 --> 00:34:43,023
Sorry, dear, if I followed you.

457
00:34:43,937 --> 00:34:46,517
It's because I miss you.

458
00:34:46,517 --> 00:34:50,355
Are you sure no one saw you come here?

459
00:34:50,355 --> 00:34:52,256
No one.

460
00:34:56,511 --> 00:34:58,345
Dad...

461
00:35:00,865 --> 00:35:04,301
I should be the one to apologize.

462
00:35:07,203 --> 00:35:13,627
This has become our normal setup.

463
00:35:14,846 --> 00:35:18,782
You have to sneak just to see me.

464
00:35:24,389 --> 00:35:26,291
I saw it somewhere.

465
00:35:26,291 --> 00:35:27,952
Joyce.

466
00:35:29,425 --> 00:35:32,530
A father should protect his child.

467
00:35:37,235 --> 00:35:43,207
Maybe this is the sacrifice we have to make.

468
00:35:45,410 --> 00:35:50,848
If only I was a father
you could introduce to people...

469
00:35:50,848 --> 00:35:52,267
Someone you can be proud of...

470
00:35:52,267 --> 00:35:54,668
Then, you won't have a hard time.

471
00:35:55,954 --> 00:35:58,690
But I'm the one who brought us
into this situation.

472
00:35:58,690 --> 00:36:00,825
Dad, no.

473
00:36:02,742 --> 00:36:07,932
Always remember that it's not your fault
that I am having a hard time.

474
00:36:09,054 --> 00:36:13,453
I'm having a hard time
because I'm always pretending.

475
00:36:14,984 --> 00:36:19,677
I'm tired of this, Dad.
This perfect image called Savana...

476
00:36:20,779 --> 00:36:23,548
Dad, I don't want any of it anymore.

477
00:36:23,548 --> 00:36:27,485
I'm tired of the image
that Mom has created for me.

478
00:36:27,485 --> 00:36:31,383
It's like a point of no return.

479
00:37:15,264 --> 00:37:17,002
<i>I promise, Mom.</i>

480
00:37:17,002 --> 00:37:20,939
<i>From now on, a lot will change.</i>

481
00:37:20,939 --> 00:37:26,778
<i>I'm starting to realize my shortcomings
in this new life I have.</i>

482
00:37:26,778 --> 00:37:30,848
<i>I will prioritize what's important.</i>

483
00:37:32,751 --> 00:37:40,191
<i>But I will make sure I'm no longer
indebted to Casa Fuerte before I resign.</i>

484
00:37:43,562 --> 00:37:45,256
Good night, Mom.

485
00:38:08,220 --> 00:38:11,990
Do you think I won't find out
where you've been?

486
00:38:11,990 --> 00:38:13,668
I'm tracking you on my phone.

487
00:38:13,668 --> 00:38:15,761
I saw where you went.

488
00:38:15,761 --> 00:38:17,929
You went to see your father.

489
00:38:19,186 --> 00:38:21,054
Mommy...

490
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:29,302
In this industry,
a single pest can ruin your name!

491
00:38:32,210 --> 00:38:35,846
Why do you treat Dad like that?

492
00:38:36,997 --> 00:38:38,517
Why?

493
00:38:38,517 --> 00:38:40,951
How do you want me to treat your father?

494
00:38:40,951 --> 00:38:43,420
Like he's the head of the family?

495
00:38:44,788 --> 00:38:48,794
Stop seeing your father!

496
00:38:48,794 --> 00:38:52,497
It's enough that we're feeding him...

497
00:38:52,497 --> 00:38:54,599
and financially supporting him!

498
00:38:57,669 --> 00:39:01,606
I already have a lot on my plate
because of you.

499
00:39:03,208 --> 00:39:06,053
And you keep doing this!

500
00:40:09,338 --> 00:40:13,844
Sir, my artist is asking
when you will take her pictures.

501
00:40:13,844 --> 00:40:16,845
We came here first.

502
00:40:16,845 --> 00:40:17,913
Later.

503
00:40:17,913 --> 00:40:20,757
The network has given me
a list for the catalog shoot.

504
00:40:20,757 --> 00:40:25,223
So as of now,
Savana isn't the priority, okay?

505
00:40:25,223 --> 00:40:27,158
Thank you.

506
00:40:31,396 --> 00:40:33,319
What did he say?

507
00:40:35,497 --> 00:40:37,669
Just a couple more artists
and you'll go next.

508
00:40:37,669 --> 00:40:39,870
Just be more patient.

509
00:40:48,645 --> 00:40:50,213
Hi, Sir Pao.

510
00:40:50,213 --> 00:40:52,182
Hi, Maxine!

511
00:40:52,182 --> 00:40:53,717
You look good.

512
00:40:53,717 --> 00:40:55,252
You're getting prettier by the day.

513
00:40:55,252 --> 00:40:56,553
Well, congrats.

514
00:40:56,553 --> 00:40:58,988
I heard you are being considered
to be the lead star

515
00:40:58,988 --> 00:41:00,857
of the new prime time show.

516
00:41:00,857 --> 00:41:02,192
Do your best.

517
00:41:02,192 --> 00:41:03,727
This will be your big break.

518
00:41:03,727 --> 00:41:05,662
Yes, Sir Pao.

519
00:41:05,662 --> 00:41:08,551
You know how showbiz works. It's so volatile.

520
00:41:08,551 --> 00:41:10,336
So...

521
00:41:10,336 --> 00:41:14,071
you really should take care of your career.

522
00:41:14,071 --> 00:41:16,573
Especially in the time of social media, gosh.

523
00:41:16,573 --> 00:41:20,376
One serious issue can cause your downfall.

524
00:41:21,649 --> 00:41:23,616
So...

525
00:41:25,498 --> 00:41:33,349
You may be... in the artist catalog today...

526
00:41:36,059 --> 00:41:41,397
But the next day, you can be out.

527
00:41:47,938 --> 00:41:49,627
Right?

528
00:41:52,609 --> 00:41:54,443
Let's eat first.

529
00:41:55,445 --> 00:41:56,880
Yeah. We should.

530
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:58,947
I thought there was food...

531
00:41:58,947 --> 00:42:02,085
But it's actually someone else's life
they were feasting on.

532
00:42:02,085 --> 00:42:04,955
Happy fiesta!

533
00:42:04,955 --> 00:42:07,000
Happy fiesta!

534
00:42:07,724 --> 00:42:09,592
Sis, you can now pass through.

535
00:42:13,634 --> 00:42:17,501
[Records Section]

536
00:42:17,501 --> 00:42:19,436
Hi, Ma'am.

537
00:42:19,436 --> 00:42:24,032
Can I have a copy
of my mother's medical records?

538
00:42:24,033 --> 00:42:27,773
Only the patient can request it.

539
00:42:27,773 --> 00:42:30,861
Or if she gave a consent letter.

540
00:42:32,343 --> 00:42:36,653
Ma'am, my mother is in...

541
00:42:36,653 --> 00:42:38,879
Liam! What are you doing here?

542
00:42:38,879 --> 00:42:41,198
Are you here for a consultation?

543
00:42:43,374 --> 00:42:46,990
How's Ma'am Tess?
Does she feel anything unusual again?

544
00:42:48,533 --> 00:42:52,002
She's okay, Doc. My mom's doing fine.

545
00:42:52,002 --> 00:42:55,539
I'm here to check her medical records.

546
00:42:55,539 --> 00:42:57,263
What for?

547
00:42:58,175 --> 00:42:59,676
Nothing serious.

548
00:42:59,676 --> 00:43:03,081
I'm just organizing our records.

549
00:43:03,081 --> 00:43:06,918
But I was told that I couldn't get it.

550
00:43:06,918 --> 00:43:11,084
Don't worry.
I'll request your mother's records for you.

551
00:43:11,084 --> 00:43:13,124
Thank you so much, Doc.

552
00:43:13,124 --> 00:43:14,559
Thank you.

553
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:16,860
Okay. Bye.

554
00:43:22,700 --> 00:43:25,236
Sis, have some juice first.

555
00:43:25,236 --> 00:43:26,938
I'll just use the restroom.

556
00:43:26,938 --> 00:43:28,772
Thank you, sis.

557
00:43:56,165 --> 00:44:00,370
Girls, did you see Savana's face earlier?

558
00:44:01,239 --> 00:44:03,808
She looks like a poor cat.

559
00:44:03,808 --> 00:44:06,944
Everyone's avoiding her.

560
00:44:07,809 --> 00:44:12,147
At least we're not the only ones
who don't want to get associated with her.

561
00:44:12,147 --> 00:44:18,409
Don't tell anyone,
but I heard her show can be cut short.

562
00:44:18,409 --> 00:44:19,991
I won't be surprised.

563
00:44:19,991 --> 00:44:23,327
She's now a liability to all the shows.

564
00:44:23,327 --> 00:44:26,897
Well, now it's your time to shine, Maxine.

565
00:44:33,871 --> 00:44:35,739
I doubt.

566
00:44:43,762 --> 00:44:45,709
You know, in this industry,

567
00:44:45,709 --> 00:44:52,790
your fans can get too affected
by your personal affairs.

568
00:44:52,790 --> 00:45:00,715
But they'll also care
if their idols are good or bad people.

569
00:45:01,766 --> 00:45:04,335
So, what are you saying?

570
00:45:05,736 --> 00:45:12,058
Are you saying I won't get famous
because I have an attitude problem?

571
00:45:12,058 --> 00:45:13,845
I didn't say that.

572
00:45:13,845 --> 00:45:16,046
You said it yourself.

573
00:45:21,219 --> 00:45:23,321
Is that yours?

574
00:45:23,321 --> 00:45:24,853
Avoid sweets.

575
00:45:24,853 --> 00:45:27,958
You might not fit
in the gown I brought with me.

576
00:45:29,594 --> 00:45:31,628
Let's go, girls.

577
00:45:35,399 --> 00:45:39,303
Savana, hasn't the photographer
called you yet?

578
00:45:40,771 --> 00:45:42,639
Savana.

579
00:45:43,908 --> 00:45:46,009
You were there the whole time?

580
00:45:52,782 --> 00:45:55,119
So you heard everything?

581
00:45:55,119 --> 00:45:57,054
Everything.

582
00:46:02,249 --> 00:46:05,189
Thank you...

583
00:46:07,298 --> 00:46:08,868
for defending me.

584
00:46:10,201 --> 00:46:13,486
I wanted to fight back, but...

585
00:46:13,486 --> 00:46:15,505
What for?

586
00:46:17,041 --> 00:46:18,851
Let me have it.

587
00:46:18,851 --> 00:46:21,109
I enjoyed getting cheeky with them.

588
00:46:24,115 --> 00:46:26,528
Via, what brings you here?

589
00:46:27,809 --> 00:46:34,125
My magazine's publishing house
will produce your network's catalog.

590
00:46:34,125 --> 00:46:39,231
So, the owner asked me to
oversee the photo shoot.

591
00:47:01,519 --> 00:47:06,222
Queenie, are those the outfits
of Maxine and her friends?

592
00:47:06,223 --> 00:47:08,633
Yes, Miss Via.

593
00:47:08,634 --> 00:47:10,507
Let me choose it for them.

594
00:47:11,274 --> 00:47:12,805
Okay.

595
00:47:15,223 --> 00:47:17,280
Here are my initial choices.

596
00:47:17,281 --> 00:47:20,106
Here, here.

597
00:47:20,107 --> 00:47:21,997
You think is it okay?

598
00:47:22,882 --> 00:47:24,850
They're okay.

599
00:47:26,430 --> 00:47:28,179
I just have a few things in mind.

600
00:47:28,179 --> 00:47:31,515
- Okay.
- I might change it.

601
00:47:31,515 --> 00:47:33,141
Okay.

602
00:48:02,880 --> 00:48:05,349
I hate it. I'm getting itchy.

603
00:48:05,349 --> 00:48:09,053
Maxine and her friends' dresses
are so last season.

604
00:48:09,053 --> 00:48:11,052
Excuse me.

605
00:48:11,052 --> 00:48:15,493
Miss Via of Escale Magazine is their stylist.

606
00:48:16,487 --> 00:48:18,531
Sorry, Miss Via.

607
00:49:16,588 --> 00:49:20,590
I'll let you know once the magazine publishes

608
00:49:20,590 --> 00:49:22,992
your shoot and interview, Savana.

609
00:49:22,992 --> 00:49:24,693
Do we have a problem, Via?

610
00:49:24,693 --> 00:49:27,863
I want all of you to know me as Joyce.

611
00:49:27,863 --> 00:49:28,990
Is it just a coincidence,

612
00:49:28,990 --> 00:49:33,970
or is it Savana the Joycelyn Trinidad
you're asking me to find?

613
00:49:33,970 --> 00:49:36,606
You tell me.
Is there something I have to worry about?

614
00:49:36,606 --> 00:49:39,008
Have you watched
the latest video about Savana?

615
00:49:39,008 --> 00:49:40,076
I'm watching it now, Borj.

616
00:49:40,076 --> 00:49:43,546
Who in the right mind would do such a thing?

617
00:49:43,546 --> 00:49:45,748
Savana, what did you do?

618
00:49:45,748 --> 00:49:47,383
What did you do?

619
00:49:47,383 --> 00:49:50,019
Who did you tell your real name to?

620
00:49:50,019 --> 00:49:51,387
Can we talk?

621
00:49:51,387 --> 00:49:53,289
I thought we were friends.

622
00:49:53,289 --> 00:49:55,424
What did you do?

623
00:50:03,041 --> 00:50:04,548
Dex?

624
00:50:10,341 --> 00:50:12,460
Dex.
